# Issue #239 Phase A — Garden Plot line-ending policy
#
# This repo targets Windows-native development (VS / VS Code on Windows,
# Razzle-style scripts) but CI and deploy run on Linux (GitHub Actions
# ubuntu-latest, Azure App Service Linux).
#
# Policy: CRLF by default so the Windows IDE working tree matches the
# repo, with explicit LF exceptions for files Linux interprets as shell
# (.sh, Dockerfile). YAML CI workflows stay CRLF because GitHub Actions
# on ubuntu-latest normalizes line endings inside `run: |` blocks
# automatically. Tools that don't preserve line endings (formatters,
# web editors, "edit" round-trips) won't produce whitespace-only diffs.
#
# Phase B — the `* text=auto eol=crlf` catchall plus the one-time bulk
# `git add --renormalize .` commit are now in effect. Any text file not
# matched by a more specific rule below is auto-detected as text and
# stored CRLF. Binary files explicitly listed at the bottom are exempt.
# gitattributes uses "last matching rule wins" semantics, so explicit
# overrides (especially the LF block for Linux shell scripts) take
# precedence over the catchall.

# --- Catchall (Phase B) ---
* text=auto eol=crlf

# --- C# source ---
*.cs        text eol=crlf
*.csproj    text eol=crlf
*.slnx      text eol=crlf
*.props     text eol=crlf
*.targets   text eol=crlf
*.config    text eol=crlf

# --- Blazor / web ---
*.razor     text eol=crlf
*.razor.cs  text eol=crlf
*.razor.css text eol=crlf
*.cshtml    text eol=crlf
*.html      text eol=crlf
*.htm       text eol=crlf
*.css       text eol=crlf
*.scss      text eol=crlf
*.js        text eol=crlf
*.mjs       text eol=crlf
*.cjs       text eol=crlf
*.ts        text eol=crlf
*.json      text eol=crlf
*.webmanifest text eol=crlf
*.xml       text eol=crlf
*.xsd       text eol=crlf
*.svg       text eol=crlf

# --- Build / CI / docs ---
# YAML CI workflows: CRLF is OK because GitHub Actions on ubuntu-latest
# normalizes line endings inside `run: |` blocks (heredoc bash content
# strips trailing \r automatically). If we ever extract those blocks
# into standalone .sh files invoked from YAML, those .sh files MUST be
# LF per the override below.
*.yml       text eol=crlf
*.yaml      text eol=crlf
*.md        text eol=crlf
*.txt       text eol=crlf
.editorconfig text eol=crlf
.gitattributes text eol=crlf
.gitignore  text eol=crlf

# --- Windows-native scripts (already CRLF; explicit for clarity) ---
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.psm1      text eol=crlf
*.psd1      text eol=crlf

# --- Linux-interpreted files (MUST be LF) ---
# Bash refuses CRLF: `$'\r': command not found`. Any script invoked from
# the GitHub Actions runner or App Service Linux startup that uses a
# shell shebang line lives here.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.dockerignore text eol=lf

# --- Binary (never normalize) ---
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary
*.bmp       binary
*.tiff      binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.eot       binary
*.otf       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.7z        binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.pdb       binary
*.dat       binary

# --- Repo-specific binary exceptions (text-looking but with null bytes) ---
# Recovery snapshot files that contain null-byte-embedded JSON/text blobs.
# Treat as binary so the catchall doesn't try to normalize their mixed
# line endings or null bytes. Consider deleting once recovery is no
# longer needed.
recovery/**         binary -text -eol
recovery_*.txt      binary -text -eol
recovery_*.json     binary -text -eol